# Maker-checker independence (rule 247)

Spec: `docs/architecture/maker-checker-authorization.md`. Owner decisions 2026-11-20: DL-LAB, T9, A-02, A-07, A-08,
A-25. Findings: MC-02, MC-03, BR-02.

## Current state (verified 2026-11-20)

Corrections, refunds and disputes refuse self-decision under the lock; refunds and settlements also have a database
CHECK; corrections do not. Front Office holds both correction request and approve; Supervisor RME holds
`manage_rme_billing` and is exempt from the branch context. This is implementation drift against this rule for the
approvals it governs until it is implemented.

## Locked target

1. Checker ≠ maker per account, decided in the service after the row lock, for every role including Super Admin.
2. Checker ≠ the issuing cashier of the invoice (A-08), holds an active per-(account, branch) designation created by
   another account, and passes `RmeWorkingBranchScope::allows()` for the invoice branch; a role or permission alone is
   never sufficient.
3. Owner approvals — A-02 LAB issuance exceptions, and every billing reversal until the owner sets risk thresholds
   (A-07) — are decided in-system by an identity on a source-controlled owner allowlist (no `env()`, empty list =
   nobody), never by `can()`; owner ≠ requester; each cites a single-use owner reference (rule 214) and records
   `owner_approved_at`; an exception expires at most 7 days after approval and cites a reason code from the owner's
   closed list (A-25).
4. Every approval table has `CHECK (decided_by IS NULL OR decided_by <> requested_by)` (or the owner equivalent), a
   partial unique index for one active request per object, a unique idempotency key and an append-only event table.
   Corrections are retrofitted with the same CHECK for `decided_by` and `applied_by` after a data audit (MC-03).
5. Refusals use stable codes and are audited after rollback with ids and codes only. Human separation is never
   claimed from account separation.

## Acceptance criteria

- Self-approval refused for every role including Super Admin; an undesignated checker, a checker who issued the invoice
  and an out-of-branch checker are refused (404 when out of scope); Super Admin outside the owner allowlist cannot
  approve an owner-level decision.
- Direct SQL with decided_by = requested_by fails with SQLSTATE 23514; concurrent checkers: one wins, one
  `ALREADY_DECIDED`; a replay is a no-op.
